course: dictionary
lesson: 14369
title: Hopeful words: optimistic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Optimistic describes someone who is hopeful and believes good things will happen. «Mia felt optimistic about the school trip, even though the sky was grey.» Mia did not know the weather would be nice. She just expected a good day, and the word tells you how she feels inside.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Here, «even though the sky was grey» shows that the sky was not cheerful, yet Mia still hoped. Optimistic is about looking on the bright side. To check, swap in a simpler word: Mia felt hopeful, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word can also describe a guess or a plan. «Our plan to finish the painting in one hour is optimistic.» An optimistic plan hopes for more than is likely. In maths and planning, an optimistic estimate is often too high or too fast, so it is wise to check it.
fact: Optimistic means hopeful and believing good things will happen.
fact: «Optimistic» can also describe a guess or plan that hopes for more than is likely.
fact: An optimistic person looks on the bright side.
fact: «Cautiously optimistic» means hopeful, but careful not to expect too much.
fact: Optimistic is an adjective: optimistic, more optimistic, most optimistic.
exercise: «Sam was optimistic that his team would win the match.» What does optimistic mean here? | Quiet and shy | Very tired after running | Certain to lose | *Hopeful that good things will happen
exercise: Which phrase means hopeful, but careful not to expect too much? | *Cautiously optimistic | Fast asleep | Completely furious | Looking for trouble
exercise: «Our plan to finish the painting in one hour is optimistic.» What does this suggest? | It uses only blue paint | It is a slow plan | *It hopes for more than is likely | It is certain to work
test: «Lily looked on the bright side and felt optimistic about her new school.» Which word is closest in meaning to optimistic? | *Hopeful | Lost | Sleepy | Angry
test: An optimistic estimate said the homework would take 10 minutes, but it took 40. What was wrong with the estimate? | It was exactly right | Ten minutes was too slow | *It was too hopeful, and too fast, for what really happened | It was about the weather
exam: Which sentence uses optimistic correctly? | *She stayed optimistic after the first try failed. | Optimistic is the name of our lunch. | The optimistic pencil is sharp.
